course: dictionary
lesson: 7121
title: Peer: looking closely, and your classmates
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Peer is a small word with a few meanings. As a verb, to peer means to look very carefully, often with narrowed eyes or leaning forward, because the thing is hard to see. «a stripy head, with high shoulders behind it» peered out of a hedge: Badger was looking hard through the leaves, not just glancing.
explain: As a noun, your peers are people of the same age, class or level as you, such as your classmates. The clues tell you which meaning you need. If the sentence is about school or friends, peers probably means classmates. «Peer pressure is when friends push you to do something you don't want to do» is about the people your own age.
explain: In UK citizenship lessons, a peer is a member of the nobility, such as a lord, who may sit in the House of Lords. That is a third meaning, so always read the words around the word first. Ask yourself: does this sentence mean looking, classmates, or lords?
fact: Peer as a verb means to look very carefully or with difficulty.
fact: Your peers are people of the same age, class or level as you.
fact: «Peer pressure» is when friends push you to do something you don't want to do.
fact: «Peer review» is when other experts check a study before it is trusted.
fact: After 1215, juries of ordinary people, usually twelve, grew in England, so people were judged by their «peers».
exercise: «a stripy head, with high shoulders behind it» peered out of a hedge. What does peered mean? | Sang loudly | *Looked very carefully through a gap | Fell fast asleep | Ran quickly away
exercise: In a group, the wish to fit in makes risky things feel normal; this is «peer pressure». What is peer pressure? | A prize for good work | A type of sports team | A kind of weather | *Friends pushing you to do something you may not want to do
exercise: Mia says, «My peers all sit in my class.» Who are Mia's peers? | Only her teacher | *Children of her age in her class | Her parents | Lords in the House of Lords
test: Mia peers at the small print on the sign. What does peers mean here? | *She looks very closely | She reads it out loud to the class | She paints the sign green | She throws the sign away
test: «Peer review» means other experts check a study. Who does the checking? | *Other experts | A dog | The king | The pupils only
exam: Which word means people of the same age as you? | *Peers | Peering | Peer pressure | Peered
